\description{
\code{mighty_codelists()} creates an S7 object for storing codelist metadata.
The class represents the contents of \verb{_codelists.yml} as a list of codelist
entries. Each codelist is referenced from column metadata via its \code{id}
(the \code{codelist} field of a column).

A codelist can contain the following operation groups:
\itemize{
\item \code{values}: values of a sponsor-defined (non-standard) codelist,
\item \code{subset}: values kept from a standard controlled terminology codelist,
\item \code{restore}: SDTM controlled terminology values included in the ADaM
codelist even when they are not used in the SDTM define.xml,
\item \code{extend}: values added to an extensible codelist.
}

\code{values} is meant for codelists that are not part of standard controlled
terminology, while \code{subset}, \code{restore} and \code{extend} modify a standard
codelist retrieved from an external source.

The object is validated on creation and after every modification.
Validation includes:
\itemize{
\item schema compliance with \code{inst/schema/codelists.json},
\item uniqueness of codelist identifiers (\code{id}),
\item uniqueness of \code{code} within a codelist across all operation groups,
\item \code{values} being mutually exclusive with \code{subset} and \code{restore},
\item consistent use of \code{decode} within an operation group (all or none).
}

Codelists do not have to be referenced by a column. Use
\code{check_codelist_references()} to check that every codelist in a
\code{\link[=mighty_study]{mighty_study()}} is used.
}
\details{
Functions to list, select, add, remove, and update codelists and their
values in your \code{mighty_codelists()} object or directly on a
\code{mighty_study()} object.

Codelist level:
\itemize{
\item \code{add_codelist()} adds a new sponsor-defined codelist with \code{values}.
\item \code{remove_codelist()} removes codelist(s) and all their contents.
\item \code{update_codelist()} updates \code{label}, \code{description} and \code{datatype}.
\item \code{select_codelist()} returns a single codelist entry as a list.
}

Value level:
\itemize{
\item \code{add_codelist_values()} adds \code{values} to an existing codelist.
\item \code{remove_codelist_value()} removes value(s) from whichever operation group
they belong to. Empty groups are dropped, and a codelist left without any
values is removed.
\item \code{move_codelist_value()} moves a value within its operation group.
\item \code{update_codelist_value()} updates the decode of a \code{values} or \code{extend}
entry.
}

Reuse of external codelists:

Most codelists come from an external source of controlled terminology
(e.g. CDISC CT), retrieved by downstream tooling such as \code{mighty.toolbox}.
Instead of redefining these codelists, the functions below record how the
study changes them. Support for reusing external codelists is still
maturing. Each function creates the codelist entry if it does not exist.
\itemize{
\item \code{subset_codelist_values()} keeps only the given codes from the external
codelist (\code{subset}).
\item \code{restore_codelist_values()} includes SDTM controlled terminology codes
that would otherwise be excluded from the ADaM define.xml (\code{restore}).
\item \code{extend_codelist_values()} adds sponsor-defined codes to an extensible
external codelist (\code{extend}).
}

\code{subset} and \code{restore} cannot be combined with \code{values} on the same
codelist, as \code{values} defines a sponsor-defined codelist.

Study level:
\itemize{
\item \code{check_codelist_references()} checks that every codelist in a
\code{mighty_study()} is referenced by at least one column (\code{codelist} field),
including columns in parameters. It returns \code{study} invisibly or errors.
The check is not run automatically, so codelists can be added before
they are used by any column.
}
}
